  m_text: "Resources used: \r\n\r\nZuber, Maria T., Et. al, (2022). \u201CThe Psyche
    Gravity Investigation\u201D\r. Space Science Reviews (2022) 218:57. https://doi.org/10.1007/s11214-022-00905-3\n\r\nSmith,
    Nancy. \u201CReinventing the Wheel.\u201D NASA, NASA, 26 Oct. 2017, www3.nasa.gov/specials/wheels/.
    \r\n\r\nDibb, Steven D. et. al. (2022). \"Spectral refelctance variation soff
    aubrites, metal-rich meteorites, and sulfides: Implications for exploration of
    (16) Psyche and other \"spectrally featureless\" asteriods\". Meteoritics & Planetary
    Science 57, Nr 8, 1570-1588 10.1111/maps.13891\n\nTroilite. Mineral information,
    data and localities. (n.d.).  https://www.mindat.org/min-4029.html \n\n[ORIGINAL
    SITE IS NO LONGER ACTIVE. RETRIEVED THROUGH WEB.ARCHIVE.ORG]\n2.2. (n.d.). https://web.archive.org/web/20180507150036/http://webs.ucm.es/info/planetas/programa/tema2/2.2.htm
    \n\nWeiss, Benjamin P., Et al. (2023). \u201CThe Psyche Magnetometry Investigation.\u201D
    Space Science Reviews (2023) 219:22. https://doi.org/10.1007/s11214-023-00965-z\n\nImage
    titled \"Psyche's Magnetometer Integration\", credited to NASA/JPL-Caltech. \n\nOriginal
    icons by Alex Martynov, Cristian Munoz. Gathered & edited in Figma. \n\n\n\nTODO::
    ADD MORE SOURCES. "
